s/install.sh`) exists and is accessible to users with normal internet connectivity \u2014 there is nothing wrong with the script or the repository.\n\n**Suggested fixes on your end:**\n- Try a proxy or VPN that can reach GitHub.\n- Download the install script manually on a machine with access, transfer it, and run `bash install.sh` locally.\n- Alternatively, clone the repo directly via `git clone https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git` using a mirror or proxy, then follow the manual install steps in the README.\n\nFeel free to reopen if you believe this is caused by something on the hermes-agent side.\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4668085669/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]